
# Flags a bare read of a variable already consumed by `move`, at the Deor level
# instead of leaving it to surface as a raw rustc "use of moved value" error on
# generated code the user never sees. Also catches moving the same variable
# twice in a row.
#
# Flow-sensitive across if/else-if/else chains: a move inside one arm is
# tracked via a small snapshot stack (one UamFrame per open chain, keyed by
# block_depth). Reading the moved variable in a *different* arm of the same
# chain is fine — branches are mutually exclusive, so each arm starts from
# the same pre-chain snapshot. Reading it *after* the whole chain closes IS
# flagged, because the arm that moved it is a reachable path — the same rule
# rustc itself applies. See check_use_after_move_if_open / _if_else / _if_dedent.
#
# Every other block boundary (for/fn bodies, plain nesting) is straight-line
# now: nothing is cleared on INDENT/DEDENT anymore, so a move followed by a
# read in later code at any depth is caught, as long as no branch sits
# between them.
#
# Also tracks partial-move destructuring (`move (f1, f2) in source`) at the
# field level, via moved_fields ("source.field" keys). A later `(f1) in
# source` re-destructuring an already-moved field is flagged; `(f3) in
# source` for an untouched field is left alone. This half of the check is
# same-block only (moved_fields clears on INDENT/DEDENT/KW_ELSE) — it does
# not yet flag the whole struct being used by value after a partial move,
# only a repeat destructure of a field that's already gone.
#
# Split across one sub-macro per token kind handled — each is independent
# and order between them doesn't matter, since every section is gated on
# its own `if cur_kind is "..."` check:
#   check_use_after_move_if_open    — KW_IF: opens a chain frame
#   check_use_after_move_if_else    — KW_ELSE: folds the closed arm in
#   check_use_after_move_if_dedent  — DEDENT: closes a chain, unions moved_vars
#   check_use_after_move_field_reset — INDENT/DEDENT/KW_ELSE: clears moved_fields
#   check_use_after_move_partial_mark — KW_MOVE (f1, f2) in source: marks fields moved
#   check_use_after_move_partial_read — KW_IN: flags reads of already-moved fields
#   check_use_after_move_for        — KW_FOR move (item in collection): marks collection moved
#   check_use_after_move_single     — KW_MOVE name: marks a single variable moved
#   check_use_after_move_read       — IDENT: flags reads, clears state on fresh bindings
macro check_use_after_move
	macro_run check_use_after_move_if_open
	macro_run check_use_after_move_if_else
	macro_run check_use_after_move_if_dedent
	macro_run check_use_after_move_field_reset
	macro_run check_use_after_move_partial_mark
	macro_run check_use_after_move_partial_read
	macro_run check_use_after_move_for
	macro_run check_use_after_move_single
	macro_run check_use_after_move_read
